   Engineering (ICICE), Qingdao, PEOPLES R CHINA, OCT 26-NOV 01, 2013},
Organization = {China Univ Petr; Taiwanese Inst Knowledge Innovat},
Abstract = {The development of new flourishing technology is offering us a more
   colorful and diverse life, especially the technology in human-machine
   interactions in which people can vividly present before our eyes images
   that they were not able to experience in person in the past. The virtual
   reality technology also helps immerse users in reproduced unreachable
   ancient scenery. The purpose of this study is to investigate motives of
   students from technical and vocational schools to utilize the new
   technology in human-machine interactions (Second Life). Measurement
   sheets were presented after bibliographical probes, after which
   reliability and validity were tested with testing tools. Finally, tests
   were conducted on the subjects of study to find out about factors for
   motives of use, which are ``goal{''}, ``entertainment{''}, and
   ``community{''} motives. As found out by statistical analysis, the
   nature of motives students have for utilizing the new technology in
   human-machine interactions (Second Life software) is mainly for
   entertainment with community as the secondary motive and goal as the
   final motive. The result acquired will serve as reference for related
   organizations and subsequent researchers.},
