Abstract = {This study aims to empirically investigate measurement indicators of
   dining atmospherics and examine the relationships among dining
   atmospherics, emotional responses and behavioral intentions, using
   casual restaurants in China as its research setting. Results of the
   study reveal that dining atmospherics comprises 19 attributes into 5
   dimensions. Outcomes also suggest that dining atmospherics had
   significant impacts on both customers' emotions and post-dining
   behaviors. Emotional state likewise affects behavioral intentions.
   Further, emotional responses partially mediate the effect of dining
   atmospherics on post-dining behavioral intentions.},
