Abstract = {One dimension of corporate social performance is concern for employee
   relations. The selection interview represents one of the earliest points
   at which employers develop relationships with future employees. The
   Elaboration Likelihood Model (Petty \& Cacioppo, 1986) is useful for
   predicting when variables which are irrelevant for predicting
   performance on the job can influence an interviewer's rating of an
   applicant. Such knowledge is helpful for organizations in terms of
   improving the validity of their selection interview decisions and
