Title = {Analysis of the Environmental Benefits of Green Building},
Booktitle = {FRONTIERS OF GREEN BUILDING, MATERIALS AND CIVIL ENGINEERING III, PTS
   1-3},
Series = {Applied Mechanics and Materials},
Year = {2013},
Volume = {368-370},
Pages = {1135+},
Note = {3rd International Conference on Green Building, Materials and Civil
   Engineering (GBMCE 2013), Taiwan, PEOPLES R CHINA, AUG 21-23, 2013},
Organization = {Natl Chin Yi Univ Technol; Natl Cheng Kung Univ; Natl Sun Yan Sen Univ;
   Natl Chi Nun Univ; ChienKuo Technol Univ; Control Engn \& Informat Sci
   Res Assoc; Int Frontiers Sci \& Technol Res Assoc; Trans Tech Publicat},
Abstract = {The current global environmental problems have become increasingly
   serious, vigorously develop the strategy of sustainable development has
   become an important issue facing the world, promote the development of
   green building is the important part of sustainable development. China's
   energy shortage of building energy consumption serious case, the
   implementation of energy-efficient green building is an inevitable
   requirement for China's sustainable economic development. This paper
   analyzes the concept of green building and features, based on life cycle
   cost of green building theory and engineering economics theory, a brief
   study of the costs and benefits of green building, build the
   environmental benefits of green building evaluation model, provide a
   theoretical basis for the evaluation of green building environmental
   benefits. As technology advances, the socio-economic development, people
   are enjoying tremendous cultural prosperity and material conditions
   meet, while the world is suffering from a shortage of natural resources
   and environmental pollution, global climate warming. The grim situation
   to improve the quality of life at the same time, we must pay attention
   to resource conservation and environmental protection to achieve
   sustainable development of human society. Construction industry have a
   great impact on the resources and environment, but the development of
   China's construction industry is the extensive development at the
   expense of high input, high consumption, high emission low efficiency
   and difficult cycle. China's building energy consumption caused by
   pollution is very serious, it brings huge energy consumption, heavy
   pollution and the large amount of carbon dioxide, sulfur trioxide from
   dust emissions, construction has reached 25\% of the contribution rate
   of greenhouse gas emissions, coal-fired heating caused air pollution has
   reached the World Health Organization to the highest standards of 2 to 5
   times. Therefore, the development of more environmentally and friendly
   energy sustainable building has become an inevitable choice for the
   development of China's construction industry. Green Building, also known
   as eco-building, sustainable building, is to provide people with
   healthy, comfortable and safe place to live, work and activities of
   space in the building life cycle to maximize conservation of resources
   (energy saving, section land, water, and materials), to protect the
   environment and reduce pollution, provide people with healthy,
   appropriate and efficient use of space, the building in harmony with
   nature.},
