   06-10, 1993},
Abstract = {Global Positioning System (GPS) satellite-based technology is being
   widely used for surveying throughout the world. It offers a relatively
   inexpensive alternative to conventional surveying for many uses. GIS
   users in increasing numbers are incorporating GPS into the data
   collection phase of their projects. Interfaces between GIS and GPS are
   being developed, and experiences gained are leading to increased and
   improved integration of GIS and GPS. This paper explores GPS technology,
   its operation, and its uses in GIS projects.},
