Title = {Aggregation of the thermo-optical properties for a rugged heterogeneous
   surface in the infrared domain: A multiscale model},
Booktitle = {GLOBAL DEVELOPMENTS IN ENVIRONMENTAL EARTH OBSERVATION FROM SPACE},
Year = {2006},
Pages = {151+},
Note = {25th Symposium of the
   European-Association-of-Remote-Sensing-Laboratories (EARSeL), Univ
   Porto, Oporto, PORTUGAL, JUN 06-11, 2005},
Abstract = {A new model describing the surface properties (reflectance, emissivity
   and temperature) regardless of the scale in the infrared (3-14 mu m)
   domain is presented. The model PHAEDRA (oPtical and tHermal properties
   Aggregation modEl for ruggeD heteRogeneous surfaces in infrAred remote
   sensing) deals with rugged heterogeneous surfaces viewed by a sensor
   which position is free (altitude or viewing position). This capacity
   will allow an easier comparison between data coming from different
   instruments (with various scales). The analytical application of this
   model on simple cases tallies with the results obtained in literature.
   The validation of this model on rugged surfaces needs a 3D comparative
   model able to predict finely the radiance seen by a sensor without using
   an aggregation hypothesis. Nevertheless, this model had to be created
   and is therefore presented in the first part of this paper: the model
   AMATERASU(Analytical Model of an incoming infrAred signal aT sEnsor
   level for Rugged And heterogeneous sUrfaces). The comparison between the
   two models shows a good concordance of the aggregation model and how
   important is the environment contribution in Middle Wave InfraRed -MWIR-
   for urban surfaces.},
