   Wodnej W Gdansku},
Abstract = {Monteiro, M.C.; Pereira, L.C.C.; Guimaraes, D. de O.; Costa, R.M.da;
   Souza-Filho, P.W.M. de; Vieira, S.R. and Jimenez, J.A., 2011. Influence
   of natural and anthropogenic conditions on the water quality of the
   Caete river estuary (North Brazil). Journal of Coastal Research, SI 64
   (Proceedings of the 11th International Coastal Symposium), 1535 - 1539.
   Szczecin, Poland, ISSN 0749-0208.
   The Amazon Brazilian has extraordinary environmental values and due to
   the existing natural resources, it has a high potentiality for economic
   development. The main aim of this work is to characterize the
   environmental quality in the middle sector of the Caete estuary and to
   identify natural and anthropogenic factors controlling it. Obtained
   results allow us to conclude that the climatic and hydrodynamic
   conditions in the region, contributed to reduce the impact of the
   population on the estuarine environment, especially during the rainy
   season. Simple measures such as (i) offering an efficient urban
   cleanness; (ii) controlling market, medical and ice factory garbage
   disposal; (iii) constructing an efficient public sanitation systems to
   promote the treatment of sewage; (iv) control the wastewater input into
   the Caete estuary should mitigate the observed problems.},
