   09-11, 2006},
Organization = {USDA Forest Serv; Venture Publishing},
Abstract = {Declines in hunting participation are of concern to wildlife agencies
   and their ability to fund and manage wildlife populations as well as
   sustain local hunting traditions. To understand declines in
   participation, it is important to understand current hunters'
   perceptions of barriers and constraints that could lead to hunting
   desertion. This study examined hunting participation with respect to
   hunters' overall perceptions of constraints, hunting participation
   intensity rates, demographics, and social-psychological data. In
   addition, differences between male and female hunters were examined to
   determine whether constraints varied based on hunting intensity rates
   that differ by gender.},
