   Publ Management Assoc Human Resources; Univ S Florida, Educ Coll; Amer
   Scholers Press},
Abstract = {In this paper, a policy-capturing study is conducted to capture the
   policies of individuals' overall person-environment (PE) fit
   perceptions. 236 Chinese subjects participated in this experimental
   study. Results indicate that all of these five aspects have a
   significant effect on the overall PE fit perceptions. Significant
   differences are observed among the weights given to different fit
   aspects. Results also show that gender does influence the relative
   importance of the five fit aspects, whereas, personality does not show a
   significant impact on the weight of these fit dimensions.},
