Abstract = {The concept ``emotional intelligence{''} (EI) resonates in the business
   world and many authors have called for more research that clearly
   conceptualizes it. Within the controversy of defining EI, the behavioral
   approach, defining and measuring El in terms of competencies, has not
   received much attention. The aim of the present chapter is threefold:
   (1) to propose a new structure of emotional and social competencies that
   is useful within organizational settings: (2) to discuss a comprehensive
   model of emotional competencies within organizational contexts that
   includes personality, emotional and social competencies, and
   performance; and finally (3) to draw its implications for practitioners.},
