Year = {2010},
Pages = {152-155},
Note = {Conference on Modern Research in Psychology: Quantitative vs Qualitative
   Research, Sibiu, ROMANIA, MAY 21-23, 2010},
Abstract = {The paper offers arguments for considering professional practice of
   students as a professional activity requiring emotional labour, as Glomb
   \& Tews (2004) and Kruml \& Geddes (2000) conceptualise it. The
   emotional dissonance and emotional effort were the main dimensions of
   emotional labour investigated in our study. These dimensions were
   analysed in relation with the specific manner in which students regulate
   their emotions: genuine expression, faking, or suppression. The number
   of practice hours students performed was a distinct variable correlated
   with the investigated dimensions. Limits of the study are discussed in
   the final part of the paper.},
