   12-14, 2017},
Organization = {Univ Sultan Moulay Slimane, Fac Sci \& Technol; ABHOER; ACDPE; GIZ;
   CIMAT; OCP; ABHBC; CTB MAROC; Direct Rech Planificat Eau; Fondat Banque
   Populaire; ONEE; CNRST; Repubique Francaise},
Abstract = {The Ghiss-Nekor aquifer, located in the north-east of the action area of
   the ABHL, plays a strategic role in the drinkable water supply of the
   city of A1 Hoceima and of the neighboring urban areas. It also
   participates in the irrigation of PMH. However, this aquifer has
   problems such as over-exploitation and pollution. In the face of these
   problems, the only Solution is the establishment of a new mode of
   governance, which privileges the participation, the involvement and the
   responsibility of the actors concerned in a negotiated contractual
   framework, namely the aquifer contract. The purpose of this study is to
   diagnose the current state of the Ghiss Nekor aquifer, the
   hydrogeological characterization of the aquifer, the use of the waters
   of the aquifer, the Problem identification and the introduction of the
   aquifer contract, which aims at the participatory and sustainable
   management of underground water resources in the Ghiss-Nekor plain, to
   ensure sustainable development.},
