   \& Hlth; Int Council Res \& Innovat Bldg \& Construct; European Commiss
   Asia Pro Eco Programme Promot Sustainable Solut Environm Europe \& Asia;
   Korean Soc Indoor Environm; Soc Indoor Environm},
Abstract = {The thermal performances of several kinds of shape-stabilized
   phase-change paraffin were studied experimentally in the paper.
   Shape-stabilized phase-change materials were composed of paraffin and
   high density polyethylene. Paraffins used in the experiment were
   n-Octadecane, n-Eicosane, and 48(\#) paraffin. ne phase change
   temperature, latent heat and the stability of shape-stabilized
   phase-change paraffin with different components were analyzed. The
   optimal mass fraction of paraffin required in the materials was
   discussed. The studies showed that the latent heat of shape-stabilized
   phase-change materials increase with the increasing of the contents of
   paraffin. The phase change temperatures of shape-stabilized phase-change
   materials are identical with paraffin. It is suitable that the mass
   fraction of paraffin required in the materials is from 60\% to 85\%. The
   results provide the basis for the application of shape-stabilized
   phase-change material in the building fields.},
