   together Engineering and Economics (ICEE), Guimaraes, PORTUGAL, JUN
   18-19, 2015},
Organization = {Univ Minho, Sch Engn; Univ Porto, Sch Econ \& Management},
Abstract = {The understanding of workers' awareness and perceptions about the risk
   management process is very important to turn its integration in the
   company's day-to-day more effective. It is reported in literature that
   the influence of risk perception research has been criticized for
   insufficient analysis of the causal relationships between risk factors
   and perceived risk. Risk management involves a procedure for hazard
   identification, risk assessment and determination of necessary controls.
   ISO 31000 presents useful guidelines for the process of risk management
   of organizations. Not being a standard which may serve as a basis for
   certification, ISO 31000 provides very useful principles and guidelines
   for risk assessment. Risk assessment typically constitutes the first
   phase of the risk management approach. To study this phenomenon, a case
   study on a company involved in solid waste treatment has been carried
   out. Following a questionnaire for the analysis of workers' perceptions
   on the risk management system, several hypothesis have been formulated.
   In this paper, the responses of the top management of the company to a
   semi-structured interview is presented. The last section is devoted to
   the conclusions and opportunities for further research.},
